Granular Execution Insights
 * Neutral Poke Control (D Stance — 48.1% to 54.6% Share):
   * D+L (Combo Punch / Mid Poke): Dominates high-tier search lookahead (38 uses / 61.3% of pokes in Master; 38 uses in SOUL). Intercepts Ichigo's heavy forward priority before armor states trigger.
   * D+K (Low Sweep): Heavily utilized in direct neural mode (234 uses in Easy) to force knockdown state resets.
   * D+I (Range Poke): Consistent mid-range Chi generator across all tiers (17 uses in Master, 15 in Balanced, 184 in Easy).
 * Special Cash-Out Engine (S Stance — 34.1% to 42.7% Share):
   * S+K (Violent Slash / Jaguar Shock): Core finisher choice across all tree-search tiers (30 uses / 58.8% of specials in Master; 30 in Balanced; 36 in SOUL).
   * S+J (Rider Kick / Secondary Special): Secondary cash-out choice (10 uses in Master, 109 in Easy).
 * High-Tier Mobility Management (W Stance — 7.2% to 8.5% Share):
   * Under Master and SOUL lookahead, ForeseeEngine incorporates W+I feral leap positioning (9 out of 11 utility decisions in Master) to shift out of Ichigo's linear attack vectors rather than standing in blockstun.
 * Defensive Economy (A Stance — 0.0% to 3.4% Share):
   * Amazon's policy relies almost entirely on range spacing and interrupt pokes, keeping guard allocation under 3.5% across all settings.
